.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The server creates a new \f[CR]forkpty(3)\f[R] session for each spawn.
The child inherits the server\(cqs environment, modified by any prior
\f[CR]CHAN_STATE\f[R] variable operations.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[B]shell\f[R] parameter is passed to \f[CR]execl(3)\f[R] on the
server side.
If the specified shell does not exist, the child exits immediately and a
\f[CR]bc_pty_on_exit\f[R] callback fires with a non\-zero exit code.
.IP \(bu 2
Terminal dimensions of 0 or negative values are rejected client\-side
before any message is sent to the server.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[B]pid\f[R] field in \f[CR]bc_pty_info_t\f[R] is the server\-side
PID of the child process.
It is informational; the client cannot send POSIX signals to it
directly.
Use \f[CR]bc_pty_signal(3)\f[R] instead.
.IP \(bu 2
If the connection is using v1 protocol, this function returns
\f[CR]BC_ERR_PROTOCOL\f[R] because PTY channels require v2.
